# Files whose SHA-256 is pinned in code must never be line-ending converted on
# checkout. `git config core.autocrlf` is `true` on the development machine, and
# a KiCad board is text, so a fresh clone or a new worktree receives CRLF while
# the committed blob is LF. The pinned hash then fails on a tree that is in fact
# correct -- the guard reports "physical-master hash is stale" for a file nobody
# touched. The pin lives in host/vcv/res/validate_glow_assets.py
# (FACEPLATE_MANIFEST["fireflow-source-board-sha256"]).
#
# The other pinned artefacts need no entry: the KiCad preview PNG is detected as
# binary and left alone, and the official DXF is local-only under .reference/.
*.kicad_pcb -text
*.kicad_dru -text
